pace{0.222em}(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1,\\hspace{0.222em}y\\ge 0\\}$, then $$\n\\displaystyle ∬_(D)x\\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2}}dA =\n$$"] [17592186134065 "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}=\\operatorname{ln}(xy)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-y\\operatorname{cos}x\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+y{z}^{3}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}.$ \nFind $\\mathrm{∇}\\cdot \\mathbf{F}.$"] [17592186134066 "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}=({e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}x)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+x{e}^{xy}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$.\nEvaluate $\\mathrm{∇}\\cdot \\mathbf{F}$ at the point $(0, 1)$."] [17592186134094 "Given that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=xy\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$, what is the scalar curl of $\\mathbf{F}$?"] [17592186134095 "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\operatorname{cos}(xy)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.$ Evaluate the scalar curl of $\\mathbf{F}$ at the point $(\\pi ,0).$"] [17592186134098 "![](images/72/7264984a1c19c247c030feae04615bb0c46205ca70475db1240db964ad6007b2.png)\n\nSuppose that $\\mathbf{F}$ is a vector field on ${\\mathbb{R}}^{2}$ defined over the region $D$ above. Given that \n\n$$\n{∮}_{{C}_{1}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=10,\\hspace{2em}{∮}_{{C}_{2}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=-4,\\hspace{2em}{∮}_{{C}_{3}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=-2,\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{1}$ is oriented counterclockwise and ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are oriented clockwise, calculate the value of $$\n{∮}_{∂D}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}.\n$$"] [17592186134102 "![](images/cb/cbe865077b446bdd97c290cef0924d3f17807a9e1039c9be45f4aa6e4b29cc3c.png)\n\nSuppose that $\\mathbf{F}$ is a vector field on ${\\mathbb{R}}^{2}$ defined over the region $D$ above. Given that \n\n$$\n{∮}_{{C}_{1}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=1,\\hspace{2em}{∮}_{{C}_{2}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=5,\\hspace{2em}{∮}_{{C}_{3}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=-3,\n$$\n