 $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $0$ | ${\\color{blue}b}$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | ${\\color{blue}c}$ |\n| $y$ | ${\\color{blue}a}$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-1$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $-a+b+c.$"] [17592186235522 "The divergence $\\text{div}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{V}$ of the velocity field represents the scalar rate of expansion of the fluid per unit of area at a given point. Find the corresponding expansion rate at the point $(1,1).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \nThe required rate of expansion is $\\text{div}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{V}\\hspace{0.167em}{|}_{(1,\\hspace{0.167em}1)}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n{{field-1}}"] [17592186235527 "The scalar curl of a plane velocity field is called the **vorticity,** denoted $\\omega .$ The vorticity describes a measure of the local rotation of the field at a given point. Find the vorticity of $\\mathbf{V}$ at $(1,1).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n      